      "methods": [
        "Every k-mer observed in any input marks both itself and its reverse complement as present, applied in-pipeline rather than as a separate pass.",
        "FASTQ reads are parsed as FASTQ: quality lines are never indexed as sequence, and no k-mer is allowed to span two reads.",
        "k = 14, 15, 16, 17 and 18 are filled in a single pass over all 404,075 input files.",
        "Windows containing any non-ACGT base are skipped.",
        "A barcode is a k-mer with zero occurrences across every input, on either strand."
      ],
      "notes": [
        "k=14 and k=15 are fully saturated: every possible sequence occurs in nature at these lengths, so no barcodes exist. k=16 yields only 4,634 barcodes, too few for practical library design. k=17 is the shortest usable length.",
        "79,117 GenBank (GCA) records are byte-identical duplicates of their RefSeq (GCF) counterparts. This does not affect correctness because presence is idempotent under duplication, but the unique assembly count is 324,126."
      ]
    }
